# {{ title }}

## Pipe tables

Leading and trailing pipes are required, and so is the separator row under the header:

| Name  | Role     |
| ----- | -------- |
| Ada   | Engineer |
| Alan  | Research |

The source columns don't need to line up:

| Fruit | Color |
|---|---|
| Apple | Red |
| Banana | Yellow |

## Alignment

| Left     | Center   | Right |
| :------- | :------: | ----: |
| a        | b        |     1 |
| longer a | longer b |   100 |

## Formatting in cells

| Feature         | Example                              |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| Emphasis        | **bold**, *italic*, ==mark==         |
| Code with pipes | `a | b` and `x || y`                 |
| Escaped pipe    | this \| that                         |
| Links           | [YAMD](https://yamd.example)         |
| Tasks           | done, not done                       |

## Captions

{caption="Quarterly revenue" #tbl:revenue}
| Quarter | Revenue |
| ------- | ------: |
| Q1      |   $1.2M |
| Q2      |   $1.5M |
| Q3      |   $1.9M |

[@tbl:revenue] shows steady growth.

## Merged cells

| Plan       | Monthly | Yearly |
| ---------- | ------: | -----: |
| Free       |      $0 |     $0 |
| Pro        |     $12 |   $120 |
| Enterprise | Talk to sales {colspan=2} |

## List tables

When cells need lists, several paragraphs or code, write the table as a list. Each top-level item is a row and each nested item is a cell:

:::table {header=1 caption="Supported platforms" #tbl:platforms}
- - Platform
  - Notes
  - Status
- - macOS
  - Apple silicon and Intel.
    Universal binary.
  - Supported
- - Windows
  - Requirements:
    - Windows 10 or later
    - x64 or ARM64
  - Supported
- - Linux
  - Install with:

    ```bash
    sudo apt install yamd
    ```
  - Beta
- - Mobile apps are planned for next year {colspan=3}
:::

[@tbl:platforms] uses a list table.
